{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Before</b> — He mentioned the heavens, which are above man, and now he mentions the earth." "And the word בטרם serves on account of [there being] two [objects], and likewise: ובטרם תחולל ארץ ותבל (and before the earth and world were brought forth)." "And the reason for mentioning the mountains — because they stand as though they are ancient, like: ומראש הררי קדם (and from the head of the ancient mountains)." "And the meaning of יולדו — for the winds give them birth, and the earth that was under the waters at its creation." "<b>And the world</b> — it is the dry land, where habitation is. And Rabbi Moses [ibn Tibbon] said: כי אתה אל תקיף לנצח (for You are a mighty God forever). And in my opinion: כי אל is an epithet. And thus its interpretation: before the mountains and earth existed, and from everlasting to everlasting You are El, because one may say of a son of dust who is crushed [דכה — i.e., mortal]."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 90, :register {:flags {4 ["God"]}}, :notes {4 "Resolved רבי משה as Ibn Tibbon by inference from the citation pattern. The final clause about בן אדם דכה is textually difficult; rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:47.156631836Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}